  "title": "Spring Egg Salad With Green Onion",
  "description": "To avoid over salting your salad, taste the salad right after adding mayonnaise, and only then add salt and pepper. Don't squish the salad, it has to stay light and fluffy.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Perfect simple and plain salad, of which I think every time I see bunch of green onion. You will only need 3 ingredients to make this <a href=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/recipes/salads/\">salad</a>. I normally use mayonnaise as a dressing, but you can use sour cream as well, or mix of sour cream with mayonnaise (50/50).</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21643,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1719232967079} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21643-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Spring Egg Salad With Green Onion</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/IMG_4247.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\tTo avoid over salting your salad, taste the salad right after adding mayonnaise, and only then add salt and pepper. Don't squish the salad, it has to stay light and fluffy.\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>6 hard boiled eggs (peeled and chopped )</li><li>1/3 bunch green onion (finely chopped )</li><li>3 Tbsp mayonnaise</li><li>Salt and freshly ground black pepper (to taste)</li><li>1 pinch paprika ((optional))</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Stir eggs, mayonnaise and green onion in a bowl. Season with salt and pepper. Garnish with some paprika if desire. <br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/IMG_4247-3.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Salads</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
